            34.2,
            40.7
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "1",
          "title": "Build Part",
          "text": "1. Build Part\r\nParts are the building blocks of Wasp.\r\nThe most basic way of initializing a part is to define t he geometry (as brep or mesh),\r\nand the connection faces (center and orientation - with a line). Parts must be named\r\nto be identifyed in the aggregation rules.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Wasp_Update File",
            "Brep"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            77.1,
            205.5
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "1b",
          "title": "Connections from Eges",
          "text": "1b. Connections from Eges\r\nAs for vertices, it is not possible to calculate directly orientation of connections\r\nplaced along edges. To define connection plane, the center point of the edge\r\nis used as origin, and the edge itself as Y-axis. X-Axis needs to be defined\r\naccording to desired orientation (in this case, the Z-axis), Connection  can then\r\nbe created with the \"ConnectionFromPlane\" component.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Deconstruct Brep",
            "List Item",
            "List Item",
            "List Item",
            "XY Plane"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            194.3,
            976.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "1b",
          "title": "Connections from Vertex",
          "text": "1b. Connections from Vertex\r\nWhen creating a connection from a part vertex, it is not possible\r\nto calculate directly its orientation. Hence it is necessary to define\r\nits orientation plane in Grasshopper, and then create a connection\r\nwith the \"ConnectionFromPlane\" component.\r\nConventionally, planes have the Z axis directed outside of the part.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Brep",
            "List Item",
            "Mesh Brep",
            "XY Plane",
            "Deconstruct Brep",
            "List Item",
            "XY Plane",
            "Deconstruct Plane"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            304.5,
            538
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "2",
          "title": "Define aggregation rules",
          "text": "2. Define aggregation rules\r\nRules can be defined ina compact way\r\nwith a text string in the format:\r\n\"Part1|Connection1_Part2|Connection2\"",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Wasp_Basic Part",
            "Wasp_Rule From Text",
            "Merge",
            "PARTS_NUM",
            "Wasp_Connection From Plane",
            "Wasp_Rule From Text",
            "Button",
            "Wasp_Connection From Plane"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            1212.1,
            648.6
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "3",
          "title": "Aggregate!",
          "text": "3. Aggregate!\r\nStochastic Aggregation builds an aggregation by randomly selecting one part\r\nand one rule to be applied at every step. The component adds parts additively \r\nover the already aggregated parts. If a new aggregation has to be created,\r\nthe RESET button allows to reset the aggregation and restart.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "PARTS_NUM",
            "Wasp_Basic Part",
            "Button"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            1391.6,
            286.8
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "5",
          "title": "Extract Data and Visualize",
